From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:49:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/34] Route Pokemon XD through the Cached Interpreter

XD's SI/JoyBus PowerPC code (active once GBA ports are enabled) trips an
upstream JitArm64 register-allocator assertion (UnlockRegister on
INVALID_REG), which hard-crashes to a black screen. Pin GXXE01 to the
Cached Interpreter (CPUCore=5) via its game INI: a correct, JIT-free
core that cannot reach the buggy allocator, scoped so no other game is
slowed. Real JIT fix (finding the opcode handler that unlocks
INVALID_REG) is follow-up work.
---
 Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
index b53f951..5895961 100644
--- a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
+++ b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
@@ -35,3 +35,10 @@ $60 FPS
 [Video_Settings]
 InternalResolution = 2
 ShaderCompilationMode = 2
+
+[Core]
+# The ARM64 JIT has an upstream register-allocator bug on XD's SI/JoyBus
+# code paths (surfaces once GBA ports are active). The Cached Interpreter is
+# a correct, JIT-free core that avoids it. Game-scoped so other titles keep
+# the fast recompiler.
+CPUCore = 5
